From ed60e426c0196bcf41887f508d0723cb479146ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:58:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(#28): a cycle through a thread the code under test
 started is refused by name, not waited into

Defect, verbatim: "A thread that the code under test starts is not on the start/join edge. starter_chain()
is empty for any thread that is not a JoinedWorker (interrupt.py:210-229), so D1 cannot see a cycle through
such a thread." A test that starts a plain threading.Thread, runs the engine in it and joins it: the thread
waits on the execution lock the measuring thread holds, the measuring thread waits on the test's worker, the
worker waits on the thread. The nested-acquire refusal never fired; the measurement waited out its allowance
and reported a false uncontained timeout.

The obvious fix (patch threading.Thread.start for good, or settrace) is wrong: a global patch outlives the
measurement, and the single-owner instrumentation guard forbids trace hooks. Instead JoinedWorker.run holds
record_thread_starts() for the span of the measured test: Thread.start is wrapped to note the starting
thread on the new one, the wrapper is assigned (never stacked), counted by a list so nesting works without a
lock an injected Abandoned could strand, and removed when the last worker's run ends.

starter_of(thread) is the one reader: a JoinedWorker's starter, else the recorded one, else None. None is
"not seen", never "none" (the main thread, a thread started before any measurement). starter_chain follows
it and still stops at the first dead starter; mark_refusal walks the same edge and records the refusal on
the JoinedWorkers above the plain thread (the plain thread has no record of its own), stopping at the owner.
The decision nested_acquire_disposition is unchanged: it was always a function of the chain.

Not closed: D2 (in-process re-entrancy) is not built (decision B3 keeps the named refusal and --isolated).
A worker that never ends (blocked outside the interpreter) keeps the wrapper installed until it does. A plain
thread that its starter does not wait on, but that runs the engine under a held evaluation, is refused too:
a measurement from a thread a measured test spawned is not a valid one either way.

Pin: no new pure decision (starter_of reads objects). tests/test_thread_starter_edge_intent.py 9 passed
(3.14 and 3.12); with starter_of disarmed 3 of 9 fail (the cycle test then waits its 5 s allowance and is
scored uncontained). Neighbouring nested/interrupt/guard files 150 passed on both.
ruff clean under pinned 0.16.7
